        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">2</span><div><strong>If you smell gas, leave immediately</strong><p>Do not touch any switches. Open the windows and doors. Call <a href="https://cadentgas.com/emergencies" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:#c2410c;font-weight:700;">Cadent Gas on 0800 111 999</a> first. Once they have made it safe, call us on 0151 558 0334.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">3</span><div><strong>For no heating, check boiler pressure</strong><p>If the boiler shows an error code or has cut out, check the pressure gauge. It should read 1 to 1.5 bar. If it is below 1 bar, top it up with the filling loop under the boiler. Still not working? Call us on 0151 558 0334.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">4</span><div><strong>Photograph all visible damage</strong><p>Take photos and video of the damage before you clean up. Your insurer will want to see them. We can also write a leak report with photos for your insurer.</p></div></div>
